Behavior is unchanged. The rewrite reads `profile` and `profileIndex` into locals once, so the compiler doesn't reload the members. It also marks the valid path as the likely one with `__builtin_expect`. I haven't measured it, so any speedup is likely to be small.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetNum(void) const
{
    const auto* p = profile;
    const auto idx = profileIndex;
    if (__builtin_expect((p != NULL) && (idx < p->numFields), 1))
        return p->fields[idx].num;
    return FIT_FIELD_NUM_INVALID;
}
```